<item>
            <title>[LU-20533] Don&apos;t sleep when a process is exiting</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20533</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Don&apos;t sleep when a process is exiting. An exiting process can&apos;t respond to signals normally and can lock-up the system for an extended period of time. In this case - if we have an alternative to sleeping, we should take it. We don&apos;t want to short circuit every sleep - so mimic upstream nfs_current_task_exiting() and annotate known problematic sites.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
